## The red thread: protect the competitive data first

Northwind's pricing, contracts and shipment data are its business. A budget overrun can be fixed next year, a late go-live can be caught up, but a leaked rate card or contract can't be recalled. That makes data sensitivity the one constraint that is **irreversible**, and the one that shapes every other choice: which use case, which model, where it runs, what goes into a prompt and what gets logged.

The TMS is a plumbing problem with a known fix (read-only views). Data sensitivity is a design problem.

