## 8. Defending the choice (board questions)

| Board challenge | Our answer |
|---|---|
| "Isn't the TMS your real problem?" | The TMS is plumbing with a known fix: the data analyst maps the tables and we read through views, about 2â€“3 weeks. Sensitivity decides the architecture. Get it wrong and a leak can't be undone. |
| "If data is so sensitive, why use an external AI at all?" | Because the model only sees one shipment's status, ETA and reference, never prices or contracts. The query limits access, not the prompt. EU region, DPA, no training on our data. |
| "Why not self-host and keep everything in-house?" | It's the most private option, but it adds GPU infrastructure and operations work two developers can't carry in 3 months. It's our fallback if the legal check on provider terms fails, and the right call once volume is high and stable. |
| "Email triage is more valuable. Why not that?" | Same score, but it sends full emails with rate cards and contracts through the model, and Copilot in Outlook already covers part of it. We do it in phase 3, once the data controls are proven. |
| "How do you prove nothing leaks?" | Cross-customer leak tests and prompt-injection tests in the test set. Zero leaks is a go-live criterion, and every call is logged in our own EU storage. |

